---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Heatmap from '../../components/Heatmap.astro';
import weighting from '../../data/weighting.json';
import { allPapers } from '../../lib/data';
const areas = Object.entries(weighting.areas).filter(([code]) => code.split('.').length === 3);
const series = [...new Set(allPapers.filter((p) => p.spec === '7192' && p.kind === 'exam').map((p) => p.series))].reverse();
const marks = (s, area) => allPapers.filter((p) => p.spec === '7192' && p.series === s).reduce((n, p) => n + (weighting.byPaper[p.id]?.[area] || 0), 0);
---
<Base title="What comes up in AQA A-level Sociology: marks by topic, 2016–2025" context="analysis">
  <h1>What comes up, paper by paper</h1>
  <p>Marks set on each topic area across the three A-level papers in each series, counted from the content each question assesses. Darker cells carry more marks; the right-hand column is the total since the first series. Paper 2 sets 40 marks on every one of its eight topics each series (students answer two), so those rows are steady; the interest is in Education, Crime and Deviance and Theory and Methods, where the balance between Papers 1 and 3 shifts.</p>
  <Heatmap areas={areas} series={series} value={marks} title="Marks by topic by series" short={(s) => s.replace('June ', 'Jun ').replace('November ', 'Nov ').replace('October ', 'Oct ').replace(' 20', ' ')} />
  <p class="muted">June 2025 is the most recent series AQA has published. AQA keeps each summer's papers secure for about a year (the June 2026 papers are expected after the summer 2027 exams), so the data here runs to the latest public series. November 2020 and November 2021 were the autumn series sat in place of the cancelled summer exams, using the papers printed for June 2020 and June 2021.</p>
  <p><a href="/what-came-up/">What came up in the latest papers</a> · <a href="/timeline/">Every paper as a timeline</a></p>
</Base>
